      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Primary Install: Python Packaging",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Rig Relay is a Python CLI application distributed via PyPI. The recommended install methods use standard Python packaging tools.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "uv tool install (recommended)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "code-5",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "bash",
      "content": "uv tool install rig-relay",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-6",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "pipx install",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "code-7",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "bash",
      "content": "pipx install rig-relay",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "pip install (lower priority, risk of environment conflicts)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "code-9",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "bash",
      "content": "pip install rig-relay",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-10",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Source Install (Contributors)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "code-11",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "bash",
      "content": "git clone https://github.com/juliantorr-es/rig-relay\ncd rig-relay\nuv sync --all-extras",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-12",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "OS-Specific Channels",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-13",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Homebrew (future)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "A Homebrew tap (`homebrew-rig-relay`) will be published when the project reaches beta stability. The formula uses:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "code-15",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "ruby",
      "content": "class RigRelay < Formula\n  include Language::Python::Virtualenv\n  desc \"Governed coding-agent harness with coordination, checkpoints, and dataset telemetry\"\n  url \"https://files.pythonhosted.org/packages/.../rig_relay-0.1.0a1.tar.gz\"\n  depends_on \"python@3.12\"\n  def install\n    virtualenv_install_with_resources\n  end\nend",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h3-16",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "npm wrapper (future convenience shim)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "An npm package may be published as a thin wrapper that bootstraps `uv` or `pipx` under the hood. It is NOT a Node.js rewrite.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "code-18",
      "type": "code",
      "language": "bash",
      "content": "npm install -g rig-relay\nrig-relay",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-19",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Console Scripts",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The Python package exposes these commands via `pyproject.toml` `[project.scripts]`:",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "table-21",
      "type": "table",
      "columns": [
        "Command",
        "Entry Point"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "`rig-relay`",
          "`rig_relay.cli.entrypoint:main`"
        ],
        [
          "`rig-relay-acp`",
          "`rig_relay.cli.acp_entrypoint:main`"
        ]
      ],
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-22",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The `vibe` and `vibe-acp` commands are **deprecated legacy aliases**. New users should treat `rig-relay` as the primary product command and the pywebview cockpit as the primary operator surface. The Textual TUI is legacy compatibility-only and is being retired.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-23",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Version",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-24",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Rig Relay v0.1.0-alpha.1 (Python package `0.1.0a1`). Derived from Mistral Vibe CLI lineage; independent version line. Upstream compatibility is not guaranteed.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-25",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "See [versioning policy](release/versioning-policy.md) for version semantics.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-26",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Legacy Migration",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-27",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Rig Relay is migrating from Vibe-derived internals (`vibe.*`) to Relay-native packages (`rig_relay.*`). Existing `vibe.*` imports remain supported during alpha. See the [Legacy Deprecation Doctrine](governance/vibe-legacy-deprecation.md) for the migration plan.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    }
  ],
